Awesome GPT Image 2.5 Prompts is a mixed-licence repository. Different parts
have different authors and terms; no single licence applies to every file.

1. Build scripts -- MIT

    scripts/**    MIT    Copyright (c) 2026 Formative Intelligence Inc.
                         Full text: LICENSES/MIT.txt

You may use, copy, modify, distribute and sell the build scripts under the MIT
licence.

2. YouArt-created content and example images -- CC BY 4.0

    The selection, nine use-case categories, ordering, original explanatory
    prose, translations, metadata, and files under images/**.

These parts are Copyright (c) 2026 Formative Intelligence Inc. and licensed
under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International. You may share and adapt
them, including commercially, provided that you give appropriate credit, link
to the licence, and indicate whether you made changes.

    Full text: LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt
    Licence:   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

This grant does not cover third-party prompt bodies or titles merely embedded
inside a README, index, generated category file, or data record.

3. Third-party prompts and titles -- terms recorded per prompt

The 150 prompt bodies and their titles were written by the people credited in
ATTRIBUTION.md, not by Formative Intelligence Inc. Each row preserves its
author, original post, upstream collection, and the terms that collection
stated for its copy:

    115 prompts received through a collection stating CC0 1.0
     35 prompts received through a collection stating CC BY 4.0

The authoritative per-prompt record is in the `upstream` and
`upstreamStatedTerms` fields of data/prompts.json and is rendered in
ATTRIBUTION.md. Copies of the upstream licence statements, pinned to the
commits used, are in provenance/.

Formative Intelligence Inc. does not claim authorship of those prompts and
grants no additional rights in them beyond the terms recorded from their
sources. If you reuse a prompt, follow its recorded terms and retain its author
and source attribution. If you wrote one and want it removed, see TAKEDOWN.md.

GitHub may label this repository "Other" because the repository intentionally
contains more than one licence. REUSE.toml is the machine-readable map.
